  "passage": "The school bus driver kept a list of students and their stops. He checked it every afternoon before leaving.\nOne day, a student named Ray fell asleep on the bus. He missed his stop. Because the driver knew the list, he noticed Ray was still on board and called his parents.\nRay was embarrassed, but his parents were grateful.\nThe driver said checking the list was a boring job, but boring jobs can be important.\nAfter that day, Ray always thanked the driver when getting off the bus.\nSafety often depends on simple routines that no one praises. A list, checked carefully every day, can protect someone when they are too tired to protect themselves.",
